@overheard rec
// W3, rec deck R12: two crew talking about the rec dec as you pass; Deck 4 above the auditorium and the regatta.

? pair:any+any
A: Coming down the rec dec after shift?
B: If there's a lane free.
A: There's never a lane free.
B: Then the float room.

? pair:any+any
A: Who left the float room on "moon"?
B: Not me.
A: You've got a bruise on your forehead.
B: Not me.   #funny

? pair:friend
A: My arms are dead.
B: Did you ring the bell?
A: I rang the bell.
B: Then it was worth it.   #warm

? place:music_room pair:any+any
A: Talent night's in three days. I need the piano.
B: You've had the piano all week.
A: The officers have stopped knocking. That means they like it.   #funny

? deck:4 weekday:sun time:morning pair:any+any
A: What was that? A horn?
B: The regatta. Holt starts every heat with it.
A: Right under my bunk.

? pair:galley+any
A: Someone's dripped pool water all through the mess.
B: Wasn't me.
A: Your hair's wet.
B: It's a damp sort of day.   #funny

? deck:7 pair:any+any
A: They ran out of numbers, you know.
B: For the lift?
A: That's why it says R.
B: I thought R was for "really good".   #funny

? deck:7 weekday:sun pair:any+any
A: How long's Pell been on the court?
B: Since half eleven.
A: It's nearly four.
B: He's had a sandwich.   #funny
